  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.9.0: The package no longer ships the library's own unit tests and no longer pulls Moq, Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk, NUnit3TestAdapter, NUnit.Analyzers, JunitXml.TestLogger or coverlet into consumers (tests moved to the Verisoft.TestInfrastructure.Tests project). Consumers reference Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk and NUnit3TestAdapter 5.x directly, as `dotnet new nunit` already does; NUnit3TestAdapter 6.x breaks the ReportPortal engine extension. ReportPortal.NUnit build assets now flow to NuGet consumers, so ReportPortal.addins is generated in the test project output and launches reach ReportPortal (previously only ProjectReference consumers got this). Drivers.Attributes.DriverCapabilities, Drivers.Attributes.DriverUrl and Drivers.Factory.DriverProvider are [Obsolete]; use the DriverInjection equivalents. README and docs rewritten for the current API; a Claude Code plugin for consumers ships in the repository (plugins/verisoft-testinfra). 1.8.0: VerisoftDesktopDriver renamed to VerisoftWincoreDriver to match appium-wincore-driver (automationName \"Wincore\", ms:waitForAppLaunch capability). 1.7.2: ListenerWebElement implements ITakesScreenshot; Report.* attaches a Screenshot payload; VerisoftDriver has full WebDriver interface parity. 1.7.0: [AutofacTest] works with [TestCaseSource] and [TestCase]; [Values]/[Range]/[Random] report a clear message.",
